1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,658
This invoice says the vendor changed banks, and asks to be paid into a new account.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,307
It's one of the costliest scams in business. Nearly $2.8 billion lost in 2024 alone, according to the FBI.

3
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:23,840
Now AI agents are paying invoices. And an AI can be talked into a yes. Openpath caught this one, and held the payment.

4
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:30,180
This is Openpath. It stops invoice fraud, before your AI agent pays.

5
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:38,784
Here's the problem. When an AI agent approves a payment, nobody can see why it said yes, or prove the rules were followed.

6
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,143
Openpath sits between the agent and the money.

7
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:48,924
Fixed rules the AI can't override, like checking the bank account on file.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,676
SERV Reasoning, only for the judgment calls, like an urgent message from the CEO.

9
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:59,405
And Reppo's independent evaluators score every single decision.

10
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:11,681
Even when the notes try to hijack the AI, and tell it to ignore its instructions and approve,

11
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,739
SERV Reasoning refuses, and sends the case to a person.

12
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:24,798
Setting it up takes about a minute.

13
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:32,308
Keep each vendor's bank account on file.

14
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:38,845
Then write a rule in plain English. SERV Reasoning turns it into an exact rule.

15
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,874
Here's how SERV understood it. It runs the same way, every time.

16
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:56,293
Same vendor. But this invoice asks to be paid into a different account.

17
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:07,891
Held, before any money moves. Again, the AI is never asked.

18
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:15,006
With the account on file, SERV Reasoning reads the notes, and makes the call.

19
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:29,961
Then Reppo's evaluators score the decision, independently.

20
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:43,244
And the score feeds the next run of the same case.

21
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:46,556
One link shares the proof. Every step, and the score.

22
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:55,985
Openpath. Every payment decision, on a path you can prove. Try it now, at openpath.up.railway.app.
